# Only the scraper script + its single import are needed in the image.
# Everything else from the hub repo (Next.js app, dashboard, tests,
# build artifacts) just bloats the build context and slows pushes.
#
# Named `Dockerfile.dockerignore`, NOT `.dockerignore`. Docker reads an
# ignore file from the CONTEXT root, and the context here is the repo
# root — so `scraper/.dockerignore` was never read by anything, which is
# why builds uploaded 607 files / 20.6 MiB instead of the five below.
# BuildKit looks for `<dockerfile-path>.dockerignore` first, so this name
# applies the rules without putting a `*`-then-whitelist file at the repo
# root, where Firebase App Hosting's builds would also be in its path.
# BuildKit is enabled explicitly in scraper/cloudbuild.yaml; if it ever
# is not, this file is simply ignored and the build still succeeds with
# the larger context.
*
!scraper/Dockerfile
!scraper/package.json
!scraper/package-lock.json
!lib/priceExtractor.ts
!scripts/scrape-landing-prices.mjs
